    "title": "pandas.HDFStore.groups — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.HDFStore.groups#\n\n- HDFStore.groups()[source]#\n- Return a list of all the top-level nodes. Each node returned is not a pandas storage object. \n  - Returns:\n    - list\n    - List of objects.\n See also \n  - `HDFStore.get_node`\n  - Returns the node with the key.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame([[1, 2], [3, 4]], columns=[\"A\", \"B\"]) >>> store = pd.HDFStore(\"store.h5\", \"w\") >>> store.put(\"data\", df) >>> print(store.groups()) >>> store.close() [/data (Group) '' children := ['axis0' (Array), 'axis1' (Array), 'block0_values' (Array), 'block0_items' (Array)]]",
    "markdown_length": 564,
